-library-en-av-oss-en-fortelling-om-norge-asne-seierstad"}],"publicationYear":2013,"pageCount":532,"summary":"\"On July 22, 2011, Anders Behring Breivik detonated a bomb outside the Norwegian prime minister's office in central Oslo, killing eight people. He then proceeded to a youth camp on the wooded island of Utøya, where he killed sixty-nine more, most of them teenage members of the country's governing Labour Party. In [this book], the journalist Åsne Seierstad tells the story of this terrible day and its reverberations. How did Breivik, a gifted child from an affluent neighborhood in Oslo, become Europe's most reviled terrorist? How did he accomplish an astonishing one-man murder spree? And how did a famously peaceful and prosperous country cope with the slaughter of so many of its young?\"--Dust jacket flap.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7355296-L.jpg","renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":72,"criticalRenown":74,"controversy":58,"llmAffinity":92,"affinityResidual":7.2,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.93,"criticalRenown":0.88,"controversy":0.86,"llmAffinity":0.98},"tags":{"craft":"narrative-drive","evidence":"reportage","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Anders Behring Breivik","confidence":0.99}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Oslo","confidence":0.95},{"name":"Utøya","confidence":0.95}],"argument":{"present":false,"statement":"","confidence":0},"academicOrientation":{"score":32,"confidence":0.9},"profileConfidence":0.95,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"628c6e07c38eb9bd8fc8ed6de4f008b7783b6332eb3e33f7467b7b4bfe83eff2","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"In [this book], the journalist Åsne Seierstad tells the story of this terrible day and its reverberations. How did Breivik, a gifted child from an affluent neighborhood in Oslo, become Europe's most reviled terrorist? How did he accomplish an